            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Personal Life and Legacy</strong><br>\nHis work reflects his whimsical and curious mind, with many biographers also noting the influence of his stammer on his preference for the company of children.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Later Life and Further Works</strong><br>\nIn his later life, Carroll continued to write and teach, producing a range of works including poetry, phantasmagoria, and academic texts.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Death and Enduring Influence</strong><br>\nLewis Carroll died on January 14, 1898. His work, especially the stories of Alice, continues to be celebrated for their imagination, wit, and profound influence on both children's and adult literature.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
